# Python & virtualenv
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
dist/
.venv/
.env*
ubt.toml


# Caches & tests
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage*
htmlcov/

# UBT state & output
.ubt/
.ubt_cache/
*.sqlite*
*.db*
# A stray `:memory:.ses` (a timestamp + UUID, written by some tool's session
# handling) was committed by accident from a repo-root shell and stayed tracked
# for three commits. Nothing reads it; the pattern keeps the next one out.
*.ses
output/
tmp/
scratch/
# Agent/tool scratch space. The name never matched ``scratch/``, so a
# pre-commit cache lock landed in a commit by accident; both spellings are
# ignored now so a local scratch directory can never be staged.
.scratch/
scripts/mathjax/node_modules/
web/node_modules/
node_modules/
web/dist/

# Design notes, RFCs and the adaptive-delivery PRD are local working notes and
# are NOT in the repository. They each describe one HEAD and move with every
# audit round, so a clone carries code and tests only. Consequence for readers:
# a `docs/... §N` citation in a code comment names *where a decision was
# recorded*, not a link that must resolve — the load-bearing reason is inlined
# in the comment itself. Convention stated in ARCHITECTURE.md, "Docs are not in
# the repo".
/docs/

# Fetched font set (scripts/fetch_fonts.py). Not committed: a CJK subset is
# 6.5-15 MB per language, and most checkouts never render a PDF. Absent, the
# renderer falls back to system fonts and the quality report says so.
/fonts/

# Generated corpus & deliverables
tests/fixtures/*.pdf
/out*
/*_bilingual.*
/*_quality_report.*
/*_visual_report.*

# Editors & OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
.codex/
.claude/
.codegraph/
# Agent-tooling state (mimo/cron task runner). Untracked, and not useful to a
# clone; without this it shows up as untracked noise in every `git status`.
.mimocode/
